# This board (ESP32-C6 devkit) has no separate UART-to-USB bridge chip --
# the only physical PC connection is the chip's native USB-Serial-JTAG
# peripheral (that's what showed up as COM3 during flashing: esptool logged
# "USB mode: USB-Serial/JTAG"). ESP-IDF's default target config instead makes
# physical UART0 the primary console (read+write) and USB-Serial-JTAG only a
# secondary, write-only mirror (see esp_vfs_console/vfs_console.c:
# console_read() only ever reads the primary fd). That default silently
# breaks this app's interactive prompts: "Ready"/"Did the unit respond..."
# print fine over the secondary-mirrored COM3, but keystrokes typed there
# have nowhere to land -- UART0's pins aren't wired to anything. Found via
# live hardware test 2026-09-07 ("I don't see anything" / input not
# registering). Making USB-Serial-JTAG the primary fixes both directions.
CONFIG_ESP_CONSOLE_USB_SERIAL_JTAG=y
